---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About — Fantasy World Cup Draft Simulator"
  description="World Cup Draft Simulator is a free browser game where you draft a fantasy World Cup XI from 100+ historical squads (1970-2026) and run them through a simulated knockout tournament."
>

<main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas text-white">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase">
      About
    </p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[1.07px] sm:text-6xl">
        What is the Fantasy Football World Cup Draft Simulator?
      </h1>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-secondary">
      <p>
        World Cup Draft Simulator is a free browser soccer game. It is a fantasy
        football world cup game for fans of World Cup history. It is the world cup
        dream team builder. You draft a dream XI from the teams of 1970 to 2026.
        Pick Pelé's Brazil 1970, Zidane's France 1998 or Messi's Argentina 2022.
        Then the game simulates a group stage and a knockout tournament.
      </p>
      <p>
        Think of it as a soccer simulator. It is also a football draft simulator
        and a world cup fantasy game. You pick a formation. You draft your
        players. The match engine simulates the cup with penalties. In the US, it
        is a soccer draft game, an online soccer game or a free soccer simulation
        game. Around the world, it is the fantasy soccer draft fans return to. No
        download. No sign-up. It is the easiest interactive soccer simulator to
        open between matches.
      </p>
      <p>
        Call it a world cup simulator. Or call it a soccer game with no download.
        Or just the world cup fantasy game. The promise is the same. Build your
        team. Watch the app simulate your result.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">What makes it tick</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-white">100+ historical squads.</strong> Every team
        is rated on the same player-stat scheme — reflexes, tackling, passing,
        finishing and more — so your picks and the AI opponents are compared
        fairly.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-white">A real match engine.</strong> Matches are
        simulated segment by segment with possession, shots, shot quality,
        extra time and penalty shootouts, tuned against real World Cup
        scorelines.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-white">Chemistry matters.</strong> Drafting
        same-nation players boosts their performance, rewarding coherent squads
        over pure stat-stacking.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">The greatest teams, at your fingertips</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      <p>
        Part of the fun is building the best world cup team of all time. The squad
        pool is made for that. It is full of greatest world cup teams. Brazil 1970
        attacked with flair. Netherlands 1974 played total football. Argentina 1978
        was strong. Italy 1982 was tough. France 1982 had skill. West Germany ruled
        the 1980s. Argentina 1986 had Maradona. Italy 1990 was solid. Brazil 1994
        won. France 1998 had Zidane. Brazil 2002 had the three R's. Germany 2002
        was good. Italy 2006 was defence. Spain 2010 played tiki-taka. Germany 2014
        was a machine. France 2018 was young. Argentina 2022 had Messi.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every name is a player you can draft. Your roster is built from the world
        cup winners, top scorers and best players of five decades. This is a world
        cup fantasy game with real weight. You are not picking cards. You are
        picking Pelé, Maradona, Zidane and Messi. You place them where they
        belong. The soccer simulator respects positions and chemistry.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can pit Maradona's Argentina against Messi's. Or Brazil 1970 against
        France 2022. The match engine simulates the game inside the app. The 2026
        squads add predicted lineups. So the greatest teams talk now includes new
        names. For a fantasy soccer draft, this is close to coaching the greats.
        For a football draft simulator, it is why no two tournaments are the same.
        Build your team. Use chemistry. Let the free browser soccer game decide who
        lifts the trophy.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      <p>
        World Cup Draft Simulator is a focused football simulator. Three systems
        work together.
      </p>
      <p>
        First, the squad library holds 100+ old squads. Each one is rated on the
        same scale. The scale covers reflexes, tackling, passing, finishing, pace
        and vision. Your picks and the AI teams are fair. A Brazil 1970 attack can
        meet a Germany 2014 defence in the same world cup simulation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Second, a real match engine simulates each game. It plays part by part. It
        shows possession, shots and chances. Then it settles extra time and a
        penalty shootout simulator. The engine is tuned to feel like real World
        Cup scorelines. But it does not copy any real match.
      </p>
      <p>
        Third, a chemistry model rewards good teams. Draft players from the same
        nation. They play better together. So a smart world cup dream team builder
        beats a team of big stats. These systems make the app a soccer simulator
        you can trust.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is a football draft simulator that respects balance. It is a world cup
        fantasy game where the draft matters most. Players call it an interactive
        soccer simulator and a fantasy soccer draft. The result is earned by your
        team, not given to you. Open the browser soccer game. Build a squad. The
        engine does the rest.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">A note on the data</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      <p>
        Squads come from World Cup semifinalists from 1970 to 2026. This gives the
        football simulator its depth. The 2026 rosters are made up. They are
        predicted lineups. We add them so you can run a world cup simulator 2026
        draw today. Every player rating is a game estimate. It is made for balance,
        not for facts. The numbers are tuned so matches stay close. The draft
        matters more than any one rating.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use real player names, team names and tournament names. We use them for
        description only. They belong to their owners. Brands like FIFA, EA Sports
        and Football Manager are trademarks. They are not linked to this app. They
        never appear in our name or web address. This matters. World Cup Draft
        Simulator is a fantasy soccer draft. It is an interactive soccer simulator
        inspired by World Cup history. It is not tied to any group.
      </p>
      <p>
        The squads you draft celebrate the sport's greatest teams. You put them on
        the pitch and simulate. The data is editorial. So the free soccer
        simulation game can show five decades of teams. It does not claim to be
        official. If a rating looks high or low, it is there to make your
        tournament fun. In short, the world cup fantasy game treats history as a
        roster. The match engine decides who wins. It decides when Brazil 1970
        meets France 2022 in the browser soccer game.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">Contact</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      <p>
        Questions, feedback or bug reports? The fastest way to reach us is the
        contact page. Send a message about anything. A squad that feels wrong. A
        match that swung too far. A feature you want in the soccer simulator. Or
        just a draft you are proud of. This is a free browser soccer game made by
        World Cup fans. Your feedback shapes what we build next.
      </p>
      <p>
        Formation tweaks. New old squads. Chemistry tuning. More replay options.
        They all start with player notes. If you build your own world cup dream
        team builder, or run a community that loves a fantasy soccer draft, we can
        share ideas. How should a football draft simulator treat old data? You can
        also report a broken save on the contact page. Or a bug in the penalty
        shootout simulator. Suggest nations or years to add. We read every message,
        even during a real tournament.
      </p>
      <p>
        The goal is a world cup fantasy game that gets better each season. No
        account. No download to reinstall. Getting help is simple. Open the online
        soccer game. Play a round. Tell us what to change. <a
          class="text-mint underline" href="/contact">Get in touch</a> and help
        shape the next build of this interactive soccer simulator.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</main></Layout>
